quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  2,84,"(Recall) when We took a pledge from you: ‘You shall not shed your (own people’s) blood, nor shall you expel one another from your homelands.’ Then you acknowledged this (covenant) and testified to it."
  2,85,"Yet here you are, killing your kinsfolk, banishing some of your people from their homelands and helping others against them with sin and aggression. Had they come to you as captives, you would have ransomed them (so that they remained obliged to you), whereas their expulsion was (also) unlawful for you. Do you believe in one part of the Book and deny another? So the punishment for those of you who act like this will be nothing but disgrace in the worldly life, and on the Day of Resurrection, they shall be returned to the harshest torment. Allah is not unaware of your deeds."
  2,86,"These are the people who buy the life of this world at the price of the Hereafter. Their punishment shall not be lightened, nor shall they be helped."
  2,87,"Surely We gave Musa (Moses) the Book (the Torah) and sent (many) messengers after him in succession, and We gave ‘Isa (Jesus), the son of Maryam (Mary), clear signs and strengthened him with the Holy Spirit. How is it that whenever a messenger brought you something which did not suit your fancies, you became arrogant, charging some with imposture and slaying others?"
  2,88,"They (the Jews) say: ‘Our hearts are wrapped up in covers (i.e. unreceptive).’ Instead, Allah has cursed them for their disbelief. They have but little faith."
